                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8cabbf36-255f-3399-bd3c-9b17c7d6e045",
                        "entry_id": "283c8a48-84de-35ab-b209-e39b5cc87248",
                        "glosses": [
                            "overwinning, zege"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0249bac6-224f-43b3-b527-f5607bf28e8f",
                                "sense_id": "8cabbf36-255f-3399-bd3c-9b17c7d6e045",
                                "text": "Van Alkmaar begint de victorie: Tijdens de 80 jarige oorlog was Alkmaar de eerste stad die succesvol de Spanjaarden wist te weerstaan"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3506989b-6b9c-4e51-9ddb-bc9e2f05935f",
                        "source_entry_id": "283c8a48-84de-35ab-b209-e39b5cc87248",
                        "source_sense_id": "8cabbf36-255f-3399-bd3c-9b17c7d6e045",
                        "target_lang_word": "victory",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "victory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                        "entry_id": "8c3ca54d-48f2-3a35-9241-9b7af2730a8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition or state of having won a battle or competition, or having succeeded in an effort; (countable) an instance of this."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c913867-436a-43a1-9576-6e53972d95f7",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "It was a great victory on the battlefield."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34702405-f142-486e-b79a-e4f56e9486b0",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "I behelde, and the ſame horne made battail agaynſt the ſayntes, yee ãd gat the victory off them: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0eac2189-04e5-4d0d-97c0-f412a785b016",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Hieronimo, it greatly pleaſeth vs, / That in our victorie thou haue a ſhare, / By vertue of thy vvorthy Sonnes exployt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b03fb9b-1bf6-4364-97b2-5cdbf4b403cd",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "VVhy ſo: then am I ſure of Victorie. Novv therefore let vs hence, and loſe no hovvre, / Till vvee meet VVarvvicke, vvith his forreine povvre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0953b311-63ef-4465-aec8-c0c201499086",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Fortune and victorie ſet on thy helme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "387daf0e-8cca-43b7-aec8-97ac224242e5",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "The teares haue got ſmall victory by that, / For it vvas bad enough before their ſpite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "771d0545-d4a0-4a7f-aec6-00dff85cf982",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "So likevviſe in that book of his [Julius Caesar's] Anticato, it may eaſily appeare that he did aſpire as vvell to victorie of vvit, as victory of vvarre: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46c29301-8554-43d5-a7d5-762d60801752",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Whereupon there was a very ſore battell: but Judas [Maccabeus] ſide by the helpe of God got the victory, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf2c172a-2973-4ee7-8024-406ca141ee2a",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "But before I went from the office newes is brought by word of mouth that letters are now just now brought from the fleete of our taking a great many more of the Dutch fleete, […] Down to the office, and there wrote letters to and again about this good newes of our victory, and so by water home late."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caac7725-997a-44a3-bb26-091f9c9bd53a",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "[S]uffering for Truths ſake / Is fortitude to higheſt victorie, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb1371b7-700b-486b-860c-5d957ca75c60",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Obſerve if he diſdains to yield the Prize; / Of Loſs impatient, proud of Victories."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "325575a2-9772-49c9-a78e-2a8fa7ff8603",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "[…] I thought he vvas not a Monarch only, but a great Conqueror; for that he that has got a Victory over his ovvn exorbitant Deſires, and has the abſolute Dominion over himſelf, vvhose Reaſon entirely governs his VVill, is certainly greater than he that conquers a City."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36664d05-4012-4889-8bea-25acb26a441e",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "He had never dreamt, hovvever, of any event ſo deciſive and ſo fatal as the victory at Pavia, vvhich ſeemed not only to have broken, but to have annihilated the povver of one of the rivals; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a68df2a9-5cd7-4a31-ba7c-4c4b692cc8b3",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "[I]t vvas his [Totila's] conſtant theme, that national vice and ruin are inſeparably connected; that victory is the fruit of moral as vvell as military virtue; and that the prince, and even the people, are reſponſible for the crimes vvhich they neglect to puniſh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee8e98f8-67ab-4654-849b-f48744c2a72d",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "[B]urn his rage / Hovv fierce ſoever, he ſhall find it hard / VVith all his thirſt of victory, to quell / Their firm reſiſtance, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2e47159-cd82-48bc-be10-dc95206b06ff",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Every body was surprised; and Darcy, after looking at her for a moment, turned silently away. Mrs. Bennet, who fancied she had gained a complete victory over him, continued her triumph."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3985edff-0852-43e9-9b93-516fe0528fb9",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "\"Farewell,\" he said, \"the only hope, which could have lighted me to fame or victory!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ff8fe9f-b493-44ee-ad81-083b6edf3fce",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "A hope, still indeed faint and indefinite, of victory and revenge, animated the party which had lately seemed to be extinct."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe7975ba-7207-48aa-8ddb-306fcab6612b",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "Already there are certain signs that politicians within the Republican party are suffering from the intoxication of too much victory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d4f391c-f91c-4fb3-b4f8-6ab04430048f",
                                                "sense_id": "293f6536-e5fd-3b57-8ccb-cf85ec79658b",
                                                "text": "England will not be catapulted among the favourites for Euro 2012 as a result of this win, but no victory against Spain is earned easily and it is right they take great heart from their efforts as they now prepare to play Sweden at Wembley on Tuesday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33e64a4c-1621-3db0-80f5-98144d765a3e",
                                        "entry_id": "8c3ca54d-48f2-3a35-9241-9b7af2730a8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Victory (“(uncountable) the Roman goddess of victory, the counterpart of the Greek goddess Nike; also (countable), an artistic depiction of her, chiefly as a winged woman”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Roman",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f0bbf69-c208-4957-8d74-1ee48bbcd2ce",
                                                "sense_id": "33e64a4c-1621-3db0-80f5-98144d765a3e",
                                                "text": "All along the Champs Elysées were […] statues of plaster representing nymphs, triumphs, victories, and other female personages painted in oil so as to represent marble; real marble could have had no better effect, and the appearance of the whole was lively and picturesque in the extreme."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "victory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92215dcb-df23-3901-8c68-3ed5343f11f1",
                                        "entry_id": "5fe5bd45-2f32-384c-8c93-57a36f504848",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to encourage someone to achieve success, or to celebrate a success or triumph."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5a2f14e-759a-4eb1-92a8-acfd48cf8637",
                                                "sense_id": "92215dcb-df23-3901-8c68-3ed5343f11f1",
                                                "text": "Saint George and Victory; fight Souldiers, fight: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61ea05f7-8529-4b98-9bf1-129eaea9fbc2",
                                                "sense_id": "92215dcb-df23-3901-8c68-3ed5343f11f1",
                                                "text": "Victory! Victory to the prostrate nations! / Bear witness Night, and ye mute Constellations / Who gaze on us from your crystalline cars! / Thoughts have gone forth whose powers can sleep no more! / Victory! Victory!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e87c00b1-3398-44c0-b30c-ade34daf2d48",
                                                "sense_id": "92215dcb-df23-3901-8c68-3ed5343f11f1",
                                                "text": "Victory! Victory! Russia's famish'd eagles / Dare not to prey beneath the crescent's light."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "victory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00eeb60f-66a7-3e6c-9595-15b1d4178832",
                                        "entry_id": "0e29a468-d125-3338-ab7c-1bf707834d6a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To defeat or triumph over (someone or something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bd81642-bdff-4ede-a70e-7d024ed2eddd",
                                                "sense_id": "00eeb60f-66a7-3e6c-9595-15b1d4178832",
                                                "text": "[W]hen ſin got the upper hand of us, and vvee victoried by them; vve vvere then their ſervants, their ſlave: vvhen vvee overcome and have victoried them; let us make them our ſlaves perpetually; let us bind them in chaines, caſt them in priſon, and for ever utterly deſtroy their evill povver: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a16eb45e-2506-4fe2-94e7-10559268f809",
                                                "sense_id": "00eeb60f-66a7-3e6c-9595-15b1d4178832",
                                                "text": "[The game of dice and ball] is near of kin, in the nature of the vvord to that game of Cock-all, vvhich boyes uſe amongſt us, vvhich Cock-all, is as much vvin and take all, as a Cock does vvho victorying, has not onely the praiſe of all, but vvins all thats laied on the match by the Abettors againſt him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
